  "macroOverview": "NAS100 printed a new all-time high of 30,044 on May 26 as US markets reopened from Memorial Day. Catalyst: Micron +18% on AI memory demand; Goldman Sachs raised 2026 US business investment forecast to 7.8% with AI spending tracking toward $800B. GER40 gapped 293 points higher on Monday May 25 on thin holiday liquidity, extending the extreme PMI-vs-price divergence. FOMC minutes (May 6-7 meeting) are due at 18:00 GMT today -- three committee members have already signaled opposition to the easing bias; a hawkish outcome is pre-priced but a surprise removal of the easing bias would trigger broad USD strength and equity selling. US-Iran ceasefire negotiations advanced Monday, causing a one-session gold spike to ~4,562 that has since faded. Gold oscillating 4,465-4,561 with bearish structure intact. AUDUSD neutral ahead of RBA June 3 (fourth hike expected).",
